{
  "about": "GegX's Pixel UI Kit as UiStyle's pieces (PIX-385). Each piece is a PNG at 1x in godot/assets/puny/gegx/ (git-ignored), made by tools/ui_kit_prep.gd from the kit in the private pixelheim-assets repo (retro-rpg/gegx/pixel-ui-kit/) and kept there under pixelheim/; scripts/fetch-private-art.sh installs them. The licence forbids redistributing the kit, modified or not, so no PNG of it enters this repo. For UiStyle: file, margins (9-slice, art pixels at 1x, left/top/right/bottom), content (where the words or the fill sit, same order) and axis (tile or stretch, both ways). For the prep: source (a file of the kit), crop (x, y, w, h), label (the columns the baked label spans, which the cut leaves out), shortest_run (the fewest columns or rows the cut may repeat: 16 keeps a page's grain), shift (tones lighter or darker on every ramp), ramps (a family drawn on another ramp) and drop (the face pressed down, in pixels).",
